import java.time.YearMonth;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.AfterEach;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.BeforeEach;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;

class ReportsTest {

    private final EmptyDatabase database = new EmptyDatabase();
    private final Rooms rooms = new Rooms(database.dataSource());
    private final ReservationStore store = new ReservationStore(database.dataSource());
    private final ReservationService service = new ReservationService(
            rooms, store, new PriceCalculator(), new EmailSender(new SentMessages(database.dataSource())));

    private Reservation book(int roomNumber, String checkIn, String checkOut, RatePlan plan) {
        Guest guest = new Guest("Bruno Lima", "bruno@example.com", "987.654.321-00");
        return service.create(new NewReservation(
                roomNumber, guest, LocalDate.parse(checkIn), LocalDate.parse(checkOut), 1, plan));
    }

    @AfterEach
    void closeDatabase() {
        database.close();
    }

    @BeforeEach
    void someReservations() {
        Reservation april = book(201, "2027-04-01", "2027-04-03", RatePlan.STANDARD);
        Reservation lateMarch = book(101, "2027-03-30", "2027-04-02", RatePlan.NON_REFUNDABLE);
        Reservation suite = book(301, "2027-04-02", "2027-04-04", RatePlan.STANDARD);
        book(102, "2027-04-01", "2027-04-05", RatePlan.STANDARD); // never paid
        Reservation cancelled = book(202, "2027-04-01", "2027-04-02", RatePlan.STANDARD);
        service.confirm(april.id());
        service.confirm(lateMarch.id());
        service.confirm(suite.id());
        service.checkIn(suite.id());
        service.confirm(cancelled.id());
        service.cancel(cancelled.id());
    }

    @Test
    void occupancyListsThePaidReservationsCoveringTheNight() {
        String csv = new OccupancyReport(rooms, store).generate(LocalDate.of(2027, 4, 1));

        assertEquals("""
                room,type,reservation,check_in,check_out
                101,STANDARD,2,2027-03-30,2027-04-02
                201,DELUXE,1,2027-04-01,2027-04-03
                total,2/5
                """, csv);
    }

    @Test
    void theCheckOutNightIsNotOccupied() {
        String csv = new OccupancyReport(rooms, store).generate(LocalDate.of(2027, 4, 3));

        assertEquals("""
                room,type,reservation,check_in,check_out
                301,SUITE,3,2027-04-02,2027-04-04
                total,1/5
                """, csv);
    }

    @Test
    void revenueSumsTheMoneyKeptFromReservationsStartingInTheMonth() {
        String csv = new RevenueReport(store).generate(YearMonth.of(2027, 4));

        // the unpaid reservation and the refunded cancellation bring nothing
        assertEquals("""
                reservation,room,check_in,check_out,status,amount
                1,201,2027-04-01,2027-04-03,CONFIRMED,779.80
                3,301,2027-04-02,2027-04-04,CHECKED_IN,1159.80
                total,1939.60
                """, csv);
    }

    @Test
    void aCancelledNonRefundableReservationStillCountsAsRevenue() {
        Reservation may = book(101, "2027-05-10", "2027-05-11", RatePlan.NON_REFUNDABLE);
        service.confirm(may.id());
        service.cancel(may.id());

        String csv = new RevenueReport(store).generate(YearMonth.of(2027, 5));

        assertEquals("""
                reservation,room,check_in,check_out,status,amount
                6,101,2027-05-10,2027-05-11,CANCELLED,212.42
                total,212.42
                """, csv);
    }

    @Test
    void anEmptyMonthHasOnlyTheTotal() {
        String csv = new RevenueReport(store).generate(YearMonth.of(2027, 6));

        assertEquals("""
                reservation,room,check_in,check_out,status,amount
                total,0.00
                """, csv);
    }
}
# Template Method

Write the fixed sequence of steps once, in a base class, and let each case fill in only the steps that differ.

## Use it when

- several cases follow the same sequence of steps, and only some steps change from case to case;
- a change to the sequence itself (a new first step, a new check at the end) should apply to every case at once;
- new cases following the same sequence are expected.

## Do not use it when

- there is no shared sequence: each case is a different algorithm (that is Strategy);
- there are two cases and the shared part is a couple of lines;
- the only shared thing is a formatting helper: a utility function is enough, and it is not a Template Method.

## Shape

```java
abstract class BoardGame {
    // the template method: the sequence lives here and nowhere else
    public final Result play(List<Player> players) {
        Board board = setUp(players);
        while (!isOver(board)) {
            playTurn(board, nextPlayer(board, players));
        }
        return decideWinner(board);
    }

    protected abstract Board setUp(List<Player> players);
    protected abstract boolean isOver(Board board);
    protected abstract void playTurn(Board board, Player player);
    protected abstract Result decideWinner(Board board);

    protected Player nextPlayer(Board board, List<Player> players) { /* default rotation; a hook */ }
}

final class Checkers extends BoardGame { /* only the four steps */ }
final class Reversi extends BoardGame { /* only the four steps */ }
```

The same idea works with composition: one generic runner that receives the varying steps as objects or functions
(`new GameRunner(setUp, isOver, playTurn, decideWinner)`), as long as every case goes through that runner.

## Done right when

- the sequence is written once, in the template method (marked `final` when the language allows);
- each case implements only the steps that vary, and none of them repeats the sequence;
- every case uses the skeleton, including the cases that existed before it was introduced;
- a change to the sequence is one edit, in the template method.

## Usual mistakes

- A common interface with one method (`run()`), where each implementation still writes the whole sequence: the
  cases look uniform from outside, but the skeleton is copied inside each one.
- A shared helper that formats the output, while each case still calls the steps in order by itself.
- The new cases use the skeleton and the old ones stay as they were.
- Steps so coarse that one "step" contains almost the whole sequence.

## Neighbors

- **Strategy**: the whole rule varies, there is no common skeleton.
- **Factory Method**: often appears as one of the steps of a template method ("create the piece").

